{#- DeepSeek-V4 (deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash @60d8d707) chat template, thinking OFF.
    The release ships no Jinja template; this reproduces encoding/encoding_dsv4.py
    encode_messages(messages, thinking_mode="chat") for system / user / developer / assistant
    messages without tools or tasks, token for token (tests/test_adapt_v4.py):
      <bos>{system}<｜User｜>{user}<｜Assistant｜></think>{assistant}<eos><｜User｜>...
    - A system message is its bare content, no role marker (system_msg_template = "{content}").
    - <｜Assistant｜></think> follows a user / developer turn that is followed by an assistant
      turn, or that ends the conversation when add_generation_prompt is true (encode_messages
      always adds it; HF's add_generation_prompt=false leaves the turn open).
    - Thinking stays off whatever enable_thinking says (the adapt-bank subject rule); earlier
      assistant turns' reasoning_content is dropped, as chat mode does.
    - Tools, tool calls, tasks and latest_reminder are not supported (raise). -#}
{{- '<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜>' -}}
{%- for m in messages -%}
{%- if m.tools is defined and m.tools or m.tool_calls is defined and m.tool_calls or m.task is defined and m.task is not none -%}
{{- raise_exception('deepseek_v4_chat.jinja: tools / tool_calls / task are not supported') -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set content = m.content if m.content is defined and m.content is not none else '' -%}
{%- if m.role == 'system' -%}
{{- content -}}
{%- elif m.role == 'user' or m.role == 'developer' -%}
{{- '<｜User｜>' + content -}}
{%- if (not loop.last and messages[loop.index0 + 1].role == 'assistant') or (loop.last and add_generation_prompt) -%}
{{- '<｜Assistant｜></think>' -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- elif m.role == 'assistant' -%}
{{- content + '<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>' -}}
{%- else -%}
{{- raise_exception('deepseek_v4_chat.jinja: unsupported role ' + m.role) -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
